{"kind":"event","event_id":10322,"event_uid":"01M2R62GTWDSYPFA991FS4FJM0","origin_instance_uid":"01M29GPTT4YE7ZYSCW8FVMKZ1J","type":"issue.commented","project_id":33,"project_uid":"01M2HSJCAB4WXJ7C6XEG23B869","project_name":"popmechanic-tinyapp-fixture","issue_id":413,"issue_uid":"01M2R5V1FTKWD13AE4FATSFKW9","issue_short_id":"fkw9","actor":"exam:4@run-35","hlc_physical_ms":1789665559388,"hlc_counter":0,"content_hash":"71382391730aa8ca4c992458d8b91c7cdd0350082ef65c3666722022a3f370dd","payload":{"comment_uid":"01M2R62GTV351VMDTREK2RZ7D5","author":"exam:4@run-35","body":"examiner (round 1): writing tests/state-exams/two-pages-converge.test.ts as the registered convergence exam plus one bun:test block per Proof leg.\n\nPlan, leg by leg:\n- (a) [M1] the spec is a module-level const SPEC passed to convergenceExam(SPEC) — that is the only way leg (a)'s 'read back in-process' can be honoured — and one test asserts each field of M1 by equality (server 'server', entry 'client/index.html', module 'todos', the two actions, the expected path, the two views, the mutant), plus that the second view is the attr form on #todo-0 and carries no 'text' key at all. The first Run: line (the sed/tr/grep window over client/src/TodoItem.tsx) is run verbatim in the same test, so M1's premise that #todo-0 carries the todo's words as its accessible name is pinned here and fails on any markup that moves the id or the label off that element.\n- (b) [M2] the expected file parses to M2's literal exactly, and its rows 1 and 2 equal the seed's rows 1 and 2 read from state-exams/seeds/default-todos.json; the 'Learn TinyBase' grep and 'git diff --quiet $ULTRA_BASE -- state-exams' are run verbatim.\n- (c) [M3] the registration itself, plus runConvergenceExam(SPEC) in-process with ULTRA_RUN_DIR pointed at a temp dir (ok true, walls.json with numeric sync_ms/converge_ms, transitions.json an array of >= 2), and the same spec with expected = state-exams/expected/one-open-todo.json resolving ok false with a failure beginning 'convergence: '.\n- (d) [M4] the fifth and sixth Run: lines verbatim against README.md and AGENTS.md — the only legs red at BASE.\n\nOne reading recorded here rather than left to be reconstructed: the exam does NOT shell out to 'bun run lint:state' (M2's second sentence). A verification never re-runs the linter — that is the Proof's own second Run: line, executed by the driver, and the rest of M2 is asserted in-process here. Everything else M2 names is covered by assertion.\n\nSecond reading: the spec names no 'assets'. M1 lists the keys and assets is not among them, and it is also the stronger exam — all three pages share one loopback origin, so serving /sqlite3.wasm would let page C reach the state out of shared kvvfs storage instead of out of the sync, which is the very thing leg (c) claims. 'clock' is spelled because ConvergenceExamSpec requires it.","created_at":"2026-09-17T17:19:19.387163750Z"},"created_at":"2026-09-17T17:19:19.388Z"}
